{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365165-mages-of-the-deep-blue-sea-black-flag","id":1365165,"title":"Mages of the deep blue sea / Black Flag","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-03T19:50:00-08:00","id":1365165,"title":"Mages of the deep blue sea / Black Flag","content":"Since reading the Pirate era in the new Dark Eras Sourcebook, I started playing Black Flag from Assassins creed and I love it. It seems like a mage story anyways. Templars...er...Seers of the Throne, Pirates...er...Free Council, the game itself lends itself well to Mage. I am thinking what Edward would be though, would he be a Mastigos who can cloud minds and be really charismatic with his crew, and learn stealth and athletics in his mind, or a Thyrsus who can hone his body to do those amazing feats of Gymnastics. When he does Eagle Vision is he reading minds, or life forms?<br /> <br /> SPOILER ALERT<br /> <br /> there is even a nod to werewolf. At one time you can blow berserker blowpipes which make your enemy fight everyone before he collapses. That looks like Basu-ilm to me in one neat little package. The game actually has a simulation of how to goad werewolves or Vampires to frenzy so you can watch the results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T22:16:17-08:00","id":1365179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365165-mages-of-the-deep-blue-sea-black-flag#post1365165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Templars...er...Seers of the Throne, Pirates...er...Free Council, the game itself lends itself well to Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>...literally my first thought when picking up Mage 2e when reading the Pentacle and Seers write-ups was &quot;Oh. So the Pentacle are Assassins and the Seers are Templars and it's a conflict between Freedom and Control?&quot; xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T04:34:07-08:00","id":1365221,"title":"","content":"Eagle Vision is described as the 6th sense of the precursor civilization, partially passed down to humans. Main characters have a far greater amount of these genes. It allows them to make intuitive leaps of understanding which most humans are otherwise incapable of (hence why the greatest part of world changing tech is rediscovered and adapted rather than created).<br /> <br /> It manifests by utilizing all senses at once, creating a synesthetic experience where minutiae in body language, clues and sympathetic connections become clear. Subjects with a higher percentage of these genes (called sages) are also able to pick up customs of new cultures very quickly. It can produce effects that seem like mind reading, but are just the result of being very good at reading the situation. <br /> <br /> It sounds like Mind, a bit of Fate or Space for sympathy reading, maybe some Prime to understand and use Pieces of Eden safely. But more than anything else, the themes remind me of the Sphinx Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-04-2020, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T10:44:41-08:00","id":1365297,"title":"","content":"Now that we got this thread started, I am starting to notice more similarities between the two and how they must cross influence each other.<br /> <br /> Mage has a setting in Ancient Greece, Assassins Creed has a setting in Ancient Greece. There is a reference in Assassins Creed of a superior race from Atlantis that gave them their powers, Mages are the inheritors of magical power from Atlantis. The Templars are looking for Artifacts to help them control governments through Arcane power, so are the Seers. Assassins can fast travel from location to location, Mages can use magic to teleport from location to location...etc..etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T10:52:01-08:00","id":1365300,"title":"","content":"Eagle Vision discern enemy from foe, i suggest Mind+Space: very Mastigos.<br /> I always seen the Guardian of Veil as Assassin and Seer as Templar!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T19:47:17-08:00","id":1365443,"title":"","content":"FYI, there should be another thread or two about Assassin's Creed in this subforum. I know I've seen those, though I don't think they were developed very far.<br /> <br /> Edward Kenway would be an Acanthus, a free spirit who cares about choice and consequence. Eagle Vision isn't a spell; it's a Legacy Attainment and all of Desmond's ancestors were carriers of that Legacy. It's worth noting that, within the narrative of the game, Edward is <i>not</i> a member of the Assassins. He's an apostate who the Assassins can't be bothered to oppose because he's willingly an enemy of the Templars as much as they are, and chasing the Sage essentially for his own reasons.<br /> <br /> I don't know how much AC lore you're already familiar with, but you will get to watch the rise and fall of the Company of the Codex in the game.<br /> <br /> And yeah. Assassin's Creed is a Mage game through and through. The protagonist is always an obsessive uncoverer of the Truth whose journey naturally leads them to oppose structures of oppression, even if they're not interested in participating in the fight. They all walk down different Paths, though. Ezio and Arno were Mastigos. Connor was Thyrsus, like Jacob. Evie feels like an Obrimos, as does Bayek. And Kassandra leans closest to Moros, I think. But Edward is definitely an Acanthus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}